  "_source": "Ministry of Education / Curriculum Development Centre, Zambia. 'O-Level Mathematics Syllabus, Grade 10-12' (2013, published by CDC) — Grade 10, Topics 10.1-10.10. Topic, sub-topic and Specific Outcome statements only; the 'Content' (Knowledge/Skills/Values) columns are omitted, consistent with the approach used for the other 2013 OBC subjects in this app. This document's outcome numbering is reliable and matches its sub-topic structure throughout Grade 10, so outcomes are reproduced as printed rather than positionally reconstructed. TERM PLACEMENT IS NOW FULLY REAL: a complete real 'MATHEMATICS SYLLABUS D... GRADE: 10' scheme of work covering all three terms (Mkushi Boarding STEM Secondary School; the source's own teacher name is not reproduced here per this app's standing sourcing policy) was shared with this project and reviewed in full. Its own Term 1 block is internally mislabelled 'TERM: 3' in its header — a real error in the source, not resolved silently — but its content unambiguously ends with 'END OF TERM ONE TEST', so the block's true position was read from that closing marker rather than its header. Matched by topic name against this file's own reliable official numbering (the source's own topic numbers run one lower throughout, e.g. its '10.6 Similarity and Congruency' vs this file's '10.5' of the same name — a drift in the teacher's own scheme, not in the official syllabus this file already uses), the real document confirms: Term 1 covers Sets, Index Notation, Algebra and Matrices (10.1-10.4); Term 2 covers Similarity and Congruency, Travel Graphs, and Social and Commercial Arithmetic (10.5-10.7); Term 3 covers Bearings, Symmetry, and Computer and Calculator (10.8-10.10). This supersedes an earlier update to this file based on a single Term-3-only version of this same scheme, which had left Computer and Calculator's placement (and part of Similarity/Congruency, Travel Graphs and Social/Commercial Arithmetic's) as a non-sourced organizational guess; with this fuller document now in hand, every topic's term placement is real and sourced, and no organizational (non-sourced) grouping remains in this file. No topic, sub-topic, competency, or objective was added, removed, or altered anywhere in this update — only which term each topic belongs to.",
